{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches instead: Traversal’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and ShortestPaths’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":". For "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" states over a finite set, number them and use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>"},{"type":"text","text":"; a grid is numbered row-major."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", once per edge, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":" (an array, a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list), so a specialized build"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" once each, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per vertex. It must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol’s “asking again gives the same answer”); this is documented, not checked, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm, as a mutating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" breaks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set"},{"type":"text","text":". Each target is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checked to be a vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yields them by count, rather than a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy.filter"},{"type":"text","text":" over a fixed neighbor list: the filter calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its predicate per element and keeps the unfiltered iterator’s state, and in the benchmarks on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1000 × 1000 grid it cost 1.2–1.8× the precomputed row (breadth-first layers, components,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions."}]},{"text":" An edge’s position is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"text":": its source, its rank in the source’s row,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and its target. Equality, order and hashing use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(source, rank)"},{"text":", unique even among parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges and self-loops; the target rides along, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"text":" and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight closure reading ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.target"},{"text":" call nothing. There are no dense edge indices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":": a closure has no identity and is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L38"},"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grid_graph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FullGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"). It is a lawful "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so every generic algorithm runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outDegree(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outEdges(chec